{"text": "Initially the catchphrase less is more had a simple meaning. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> First mentioned in Robert Brownings poem Andrea del Sarto, it suggests that everything simple is better and more beautiful than the complex and tangled. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Nowadays this phrase is heard often, maybe even too often. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> But it is important to recognize that the way of thinking that lies behind these words slowly extinguishes certain habits from our daily life. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> For example, think about the heavy, massive radio receivers that existed back in the day. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Over time, many of their buttons became viewed as extra and were removed, and with each reduction these devices eventually developed into the phones in our pockets. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The scale of the object became smaller, and the functions of the buttons got lost in the three dot menus and multilayered folders of our phones.", "alignment": {"characters": ["I", "n", "i", "t", "i", "a", "l", "l", "y", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "c", "a", "t", "c", "h", "p", "h", "r", "a", "s", "e", " ", "l", "e", "s", "s", " ", "i", "s", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "h", "a", "d", " ", "a", " ", "s", "i", "m", "p", "l", "e", " ", "m", "e", "a", "n", "i", "n", "g", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "F", "i", "r", "s", "t", " ", "m", "e", "n", "t", "i", "o", "n", "e", "d", " ", "i", "n", " ", "R", "o", "b", "e", "r", "t", " ", "B", "r", "o", "w", "n", "i", "n", "g", "s", " ", "p", "o", "e", "m", " ", "A", "n", "d", "r", "e", "a", " ", "d", "e", "l", " ", "S", "a", "r", "t", "o", ",", " ", "i", "t", " ", "s", "u", "g", "g", "e", "s", "t", "s", " ", "t", "h", "a", "t", " ", "e", "v", "e", "r", "y", "t", "h", "i", "n", "g", " ", "s", "i", "m", "p", "l", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "b", "e", "t", "t", "e", "r", " ", "a", "n", "d", " ", "m", "o", "r", "e", " ", "b", "e", "a", "u